      "name": "schema",
      "description": "Return the universal-link database schema — every table with its columns, types, and approximate row counts, plus analyst notes on how the tables relate. Call this FIRST to learn what you can query, then use the `query` tool. Tables live in the \"universal_link\" pg schema and raw SQL must schema-qualify them (e.g. universal_link.click_events).",
