    {
      "name": "query",
      "description": "Run a single READ-ONLY SQL statement (SELECT or WITH) against the universal-link Postgres database and return the rows. Use `schema` first to discover tables/columns. IMPORTANT: schema-qualify every table (e.g. universal_link.click_events) — the search_path does not include the app schema. Timestamps are stored in UTC. Only one statement is allowed; writes/DDL are rejected at the DB level. Returns { row_count, truncated, rows }; on a bad query it returns { error } so you can fix the SQL and retry.",
