  "protocolVersion": null,
  "instructions": "HumanlabsLink MCP — self-hosted deep-link & attribution engine (Branch/AppsFlyer alternative). Tools manage first-party apps, deep links, templates, webhooks, analytics, and SDK integration. Multi-app model: each app has a `slug`; short links are `https://<domain>/<slug>/<code>`, and an in-app destination is the link's `deepLinkPath` (set at creation, NOT extra URL path segments). Links are created server-side via these tools — mobile SDKs only RECEIVE links (deferred + direct). SDKs install from public registries (npm @humanlabs-kr/link-expo-sdk, CocoaPods HumanlabsLinkSDK, Maven Central world.humanlabs:link-sdk); use get_sdk_install_snippet for ready-to-paste setup. Auth is a Cloudflare Access service token (single-tenant) — not a per-workspace API key.",
  "durationMs": 7391,
  "stderr": "[universal-link-mcp] Warning: no auth configured. Set CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID + CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET (Cloudflare Access service token) — or HUMANLABSLINK_API_KEY. Proceeding unauthenticated; control-plane calls will 401 if the API is protected.\n[humanlabs-link-mcp] Connected (stdio). 15 tools available. Base URL: https://link.humanlabs.world/api\n"
